# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) once a phase needs the API — the client arrives in
# Phase E. Expo exposes only variables prefixed with EXPO_PUBLIC_ to the app.
#
# Include the /api suffix; the API's routes all live under it.
#
#   Android emulator on this PC:      http://10.0.2.2:8001/api
#   Real phone on the same Wi-Fi:     http://<PC LAN address>:8001/api
#   (find it with:  ipconfig  →  IPv4 Address, e.g. http://192.168.254.105:8001/api)
#
# The API has to be started so the phone can reach it:
#   cd backend; php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8001
# and Windows Firewall needs an inbound rule for TCP 8001 (see README.md).
#
#   Phone over USB (adb reverse, works when Wi-Fi cannot reach this PC):
#       adb reverse tcp:8001 tcp:8001     # then start Metro with: npx expo start --localhost
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8001/api
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SESSION_TTL_DAYS is optional and only for testing the session-expiry screen:
# the app already uses 30 days, the same lifetime backend/config/sanctum.php enforces.
# It is baked in at build time, so a value of 0.002 (about three minutes) means a test
# build where every session expires almost immediately — never set it for real use.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SESSION_TTL_DAYS=0.002
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.254.105:8001/api
